course: dictionary
lesson: 10142
title: Thrilling and the power of context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Brain myths are thrilling: a tongue with neat taste zones, people born "right-brained" or "not maths people", Mozart making babies brainy, eyeballs popping out if you sneeze with them open, French learned from tapes under your pillow.» The list after the colon gives the clues. These are surprising, amazing claims, so thrilling must describe something that makes you want to keep reading.
explain: Thrilling means very exciting, with a strong, happy rush of feeling. Here it is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like a thrilling ride or a thrilling match. Check by swapping in exciting: «Brain myths are exciting» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Thrilling can also be the -ing form of the verb thrill. «The magician was thrilling the crowd» means the magician was making the crowd feel excited. Ask yourself: is the word describing a thing, or is someone doing something to someone else? That tells you which form you are reading.
fact: Thrilling means very exciting, with a strong, happy rush of excitement.
fact: «A thrilling finish» means the end of a race or match is full of excitement.
fact: Thrill is also a verb: to thrill someone means to make them feel very excited.
fact: Book blurbs and reviews often use «thrilling» to tell you a story is full of suspense.
fact: A good check is to swap in exciting: if the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
exercise: «The roller coaster was thrilling, with a drop that made everyone scream.» What does thrilling mean here? | Quiet and calm | Very slow and boring | Wet from the rain | *Very exciting
exercise: «The magician was thrilling the crowd.» Here thrilling is a verb form. What does it mean? | Telling the crowd to go home | Hiding from the crowd | *Making the crowd feel excited | Standing still while the crowd watched
exercise: Ella says a thrilling book is a boring book. Is she right? | Yes, because long books are always boring | Yes, thrilling means boring | Only if the book is about a tongue | *No, thrilling means very exciting
test: «The final goal in the match was thrilling to watch.» Which word could replace thrilling without changing the meaning? | Quiet | Muddy | *Exciting | Dull
test: Which word could replace thrilling in «a thrilling adventure» without changing the meaning? | Cold | Tiny | Sleepy | *Exciting
exam: «Brain myths are thrilling.» What is the best meaning of thrilling in this sentence? | Very wet and grey | Very sad and tired | *Very exciting, surprising enough to make you read on | Very old and dusty
